Three changes to pristine rhubarb-lip-sync 1.14.0, all of them about turning a
one-shot CLI into a resident service. Nothing here alters what Rhubarb decides;
`animate()` and both recognizers are untouched.

  1. CMakeLists.txt — build our `avatarsync` executable from src/avatarsync/.
  2. pocketSphinxTools.cpp — cache the decoder pool across calls
     (RHUBARB_WARM_POOL). Upstream rebuilds it per call, which is right for a
     process that runs once and exits and ruinous for a service: ps_init()
     against an 82 MB acoustic model dominates every short clip. Measured 181 ms
     cold → 31 ms warm for `phonetic`.
  3. pocketSphinxTools.cpp — let RHUBARB_RES_DIR override the model directory.
     Upstream derives it from the executable's own location, which forces one
     56 MB copy of the models per platform binary; we keep a single shared tree.

--- a/rhubarb/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/rhubarb/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -518,7 +518,25 @@
 	rhubarb-lib
 )
 target_compile_options(rhubarb PUBLIC ${enableWarningsFlags})
+
+# Define the avatarsync executable: one resident process serving both viseme
+# legs — text+duration -> cues with no audio (rhubarb-recognition for
+# tokenizeText/wordToPhones plus rhubarb-animation's animate(), never touching
+# the acoustic model), and real `phonetic` recognition over PCM handed in on
+# stdin (rhubarb-lib's animateAudioClip).
+add_executable(avatarsync
+	src/avatarsync/avatarsync.cpp
+)
+target_link_libraries(avatarsync
+	rhubarb-lib
+	rhubarb-animation
+	rhubarb-recognition
+	rhubarb-core
+	rhubarb-time
+	rhubarb-logging
+	rhubarb-tools
+)

 # Define test project
 set(TEST_FILES
 	tests/stringToolsTests.cpp
--- a/rhubarb/src/recognition/pocketSphinxTools.cpp
+++ b/rhubarb/src/recognition/pocketSphinxTools.cpp
@@ -1,6 +1,9 @@
 #include "pocketSphinxTools.h"

 #include "tools/platformTools.h"
